Page 1144 wanànu: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* [[wanàno]], [[wonanno]]

===Etymology===
Literally '''his cheek'''. This word is a third person singular possessive of a ''dependent'' noun. That means that it is based on a bound lemma /-anànu-/, only appearing in compounds with affixes.

Cognate with {{cog|umu|wánuw||his cheek}}, {{cog|xpq|wanonaw||his cheek}}, {{cog|wam|wannônaw||his cheek}}.

===Noun===
{{head|unm|noun|g=in|plural|wanànuwa}}

# [[cheek]]

===References===
* {{R:unm:LTD|wanànu}}
-------- end text --------
