A late 1700s variant (possibly Munsee) ''''ptáhoweu'''' (''he catches fish with a rod'') is a clear cognate with {{cog|umu|ptáheew||he hooks fish}}, {{cog|wam|puttawhau||he catches (fish) by a snare}}, and more distantly with {{cog|pqm|ptahma||he hooks fish}} and {{cog|aaq|pə́thame||he catches fish by hook}}. {{rfe|unm}}

